---
layout: layouts/base.njk
title: Sébastien Boulnois, PhD | Human Factors & Human-Systems Integration Engineer
description: Human factors and HSI engineer with a PhD in aviation human-centered design, bringing together human performance, usability, accessibility and user experience research, from cockpit simulators to nuclear plants. US citizen, eligible for Secret/TS.
---
<section class="hero" aria-labelledby="hero-title">
  <div class="container hero__inner">
    <div class="hero__text">
      <p class="eyebrow">{{ site.title }}</p>
      <h1 class="hero__title" id="hero-title">I design systems around the people who run them: the right information, at the right time, in the right format.</h1>
      <p class="hero__lead">People do their best work when the system fits how they work and decide. For more than ten years I've studied how airline pilots, plant workers, firefighters and everyday users make decisions, and designed around them. I combine human performance measures with usability, accessibility and user experience research, and I'm now bringing that work back to safety-critical systems.</p>
      <ul class="status-list" aria-label="Availability">
        <li class="status-list__item">US citizen, eligible for Secret/TS</li>
        <li class="status-list__item">Palmdale, San Diego or remote</li>
        <li class="status-list__item">Available now</li>
      </ul>
      <div class="button-group">
        <a class="button button--primary" href="{{ site.resume }}" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Download resume <span class="button__meta">(PDF)</span><span class="visually-hidden">, opens in a new tab</span>{% include "partials/new-tab-icon.njk" %}</a>
        <a class="button button--secondary" href="mailto:{{ site.email }}">Email me</a>
      </div>
    </div>
    <picture class="hero__portrait">
      <source type="image/webp" srcset="assets/images/sebastien-boulnois-portrait-480.webp 480w, assets/images/sebastien-boulnois-portrait-700.webp 700w, assets/images/sebastien-boulnois-portrait-1200.webp 1200w" sizes="(min-width: 60rem) 22rem, 80vw">
      <img src="assets/images/sebastien-boulnois-portrait-480.jpg" srcset="assets/images/sebastien-boulnois-portrait-480.jpg 480w, assets/images/sebastien-boulnois-portrait-700.jpg 700w, assets/images/sebastien-boulnois-portrait-1200.jpg 1200w" sizes="(min-width: 60rem) 22rem, 80vw" class="hero__image" width="480" height="600" alt="Portrait of Sébastien Boulnois smiling, wearing glasses and a light blue shirt.">
    </picture>
  </div>
</section>


<section class="section" id="work" aria-labelledby="work-title">
  <div class="container">
    <h2 class="section__title" id="work-title">Selected work</h2>
    <ul class="case-list">
      {%- for case in work %}
      <li class="case-card">
        <p class="case-card__meta">{{ case.context }} · {{ case.years }}</p>
        <h3 class="case-card__title">
          {%- if case.url %}<a class="case-card__link" href="{{ case.url }}">{{ case.title }}</a>{% else %}{{ case.title }}{% endif -%}
        </h3>
        <p class="case-card__summary">{{ case.summary }}</p>
        <ul class="tag-list" aria-label="At a glance: field, role, scope and outcome">
          {%- for fact in case.facts %}
          <li class="tag-list__item">{{ fact }}</li>
          {%- endfor %}
        </ul>
      </li>
      {%- endfor %}
    </ul>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section section--alt" aria-labelledby="methods-title">
  <div class="container media-split">
    <div class="media-split__text">
      <h2 class="section__title" id="methods-title">How I work</h2>
      <dl class="method-list">
        <div class="method-list__item">
          <dt class="method-list__term">Human performance measurement</dt>
          <dd class="method-list__detail">Workload, situation awareness and decision-making, measured with NASA-TLX, CC-SART and SAGAT-style probes.</dd>
        </div>
        <div class="method-list__item">
          <dt class="method-list__term">Usability, accessibility and user experience</dt>
          <dd class="method-list__detail">Usability testing, heuristic evaluation and accessibility review, so information is easy to find, read and act on under pressure.</dd>
        </div>
        <div class="method-list__item">
          <dt class="method-list__term">Human-in-the-loop testing</dt>
          <dd class="method-list__detail">Realistic scenarios and pilot-in-the-loop studies in Boeing 737 and Airbus A320 simulators, to see how a design holds up before it reaches the field.</dd>
        </div>
        <div class="method-list__item">
          <dt class="method-list__term">Cognitive task analysis</dt>
          <dd class="method-list__detail">Expert interviews and field observation to find where decisions break down, and why.</dd>
        </div>
        <div class="method-list__item">
          <dt class="method-list__term">Human-machine teaming</dt>
          <dd class="method-list__detail">How people and robots share a task and stay aware of each other, from manual control to full autonomy.</dd>
        </div>
      </dl>
    </div>
    <figure class="media-split__figure">
      <picture>
        <source type="image/webp" srcset="assets/images/b737-simulator-study-800.webp 800w, assets/images/b737-simulator-study-1600.webp 1600w" sizes="(min-width: 60rem) 34rem, 92vw">
        <img src="assets/images/b737-simulator-study-800.jpg" srcset="assets/images/b737-simulator-study-800.jpg 800w, assets/images/b737-simulator-study-1600.jpg 1600w" sizes="(min-width: 60rem) 34rem, 92vw" class="media-split__image" width="800" height="532" loading="lazy" alt="Sébastien running a study session with a participant at the controls of a Boeing 737 cockpit simulator.">
      </picture>
      <figcaption class="media-split__caption">Pilot-in-the-loop testing in a Boeing 737 simulator, Florida Tech.</figcaption>
    </figure>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section" id="about" aria-labelledby="about-title">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="prose">
    <h2 class="section__title section__title--compact" id="about-title">About</h2>
    <p>I started in aviation human factors, studying how pilots make decisions in cockpit simulators, and took that into field research in nuclear power plants. I then spent five years leading research for Fortune 500 clients, where I learned to deliver findings that engineers and executives act on.</p>
    <p>In 2024 I took a planned break to care for my young children. I’m now returning to the work I trained for: systems where human performance has real consequences.</p>
    <p class="prose__note">Supported the INCOSE Human-Systems Integration Workshop, 2015–2018. French (native) and English.</p>
    <p><a href="about/">More about my background and how I work</a></p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
